<div class="app">

<div class="kpis four" id="kpis">
  <div class="kpi hero">
    <div class="k">You're allocating</div>
    <div class="v" id="kSave">$0</div>
    <div class="s" id="kSaveSub">per year</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="k"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--gold)"></span>Government gives back</div>
    <div class="v" id="kBack">$0</div>
    <div class="s" id="kBackSub">in year one</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="k"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--claw)"></span>Effective marginal rate</div>
    <div class="v" id="kEmr">0%</div>
    <div class="s" id="kEmrSub">—</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="k">Return on what you save</div>
    <div class="v" id="kRoi">—</div>
    <div class="s" id="kRoiSub">first-year value</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="workspace">

<aside class="rail">
  <details class="grp" open>
    <summary>Your income</summary>
    <div class="grpbody">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="income">Employment income</label>
        <input type="number" id="income" value="68000" min="0" max="500000" step="1000">
        <input type="range" id="incomeRange" value="68000" min="15000" max="250000" step="500" aria-label="Income">
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label>Household</label>
        <div class="seg-ctl" id="marital">
          <button type="button" data-v="single" aria-pressed="true">Single</button>
          <button type="button" data-v="couple" aria-pressed="false">Partnered</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="field" id="partnerField" hidden>
        <label for="partner">Partner's income</label>
        <input type="number" id="partner" value="55000" min="0" max="500000" step="1000">
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label>Children under 18</label>
        <div class="seg-ctl" id="haskids">
          <button type="button" data-v="no" aria-pressed="true">None</button>
          <button type="button" data-v="yes" aria-pressed="false">I have children</button>
        </div>
        <div id="kidsWrap" hidden>
          <div class="kids" id="kids"></div>
          <div class="hint">Children change the answer: benefit clawback raises the value of every deduction.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="grp" open>
    <summary>What you can save</summary>
    <div class="grpbody">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="save">Monthly savings</label>
        <input type="number" id="save" value="500" min="0" max="20000" step="50">
        <div class="hint">This is the amount being allocated below.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="grp" open>
    <summary>Accounts available</summary>
    <div class="grpbody">
      <div class="field">
        <label class="row" style="gap:8px;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">
          <input type="checkbox" id="fhsa" checked style="accent-color:var(--stat)">
          <span>I could buy a first home someday</span>
        </label>
        <div class="hint">Unlocks the FHSA — deductible going in and tax-free coming out.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label class="row" style="gap:8px;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px">
          <input type="checkbox" id="hasMatch" style="accent-color:var(--stat)">
          <span>My employer matches my retirement contributions</span>
        </label>
        <div id="matchWrap" hidden>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top:9px">
            <input type="number" id="matchRate" value="50" min="0" max="200" step="5" aria-label="Cents matched per dollar">
            <span class="hint" style="margin:0;white-space:nowrap">¢ per $1, up to</span>
            <input type="number" id="matchCap" value="3000" min="0" max="50000" step="500" aria-label="Most the employer will match per year">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="retrate">Expected tax rate when you withdraw</label>
        <div class="row">
          <input type="range" id="retrate" value="25" min="0" max="55" step="1" style="flex:1">
          <span class="num" id="retrateOut" style="width:52px;text-align:right;font-weight:600">25%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hint">The RRSP decision turns entirely on this. Below your current
        effective rate, an RRSP gains; above it, an RRSP loses.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="grp">
    <summary>Share</summary>
    <div class="grpbody">
      <div class="btnrow">
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="copyLink">Copy link to these inputs</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="doPrint">Print</button>
      </div>
      <div class="assum" id="shareMsg">Every input is encoded in the address bar, so a link
      reproduces this exact allocation. Nothing is uploaded.</div>
    </div>
  </details>
</aside>

<main style="min-width:0">
  <div class="tabpanel" style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:7px">
    <div class="block" style="padding:0">
      <div class="block-h" style="padding:16px 18px 0;margin-bottom:8px">
        <h3>Where your money should go, in order</h3>
        <span class="sub">Highest marginal value first</span>
      </div>
      <div id="alloc"></div>
      <div class="bd" id="allocNote" hidden></div>
    </div>
    <div class="total">
      <span class="k">What the government gives back in year one</span>
      <span><span class="v" id="totalVal">$0</span> <span class="k" id="totalPct"></span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="bd" id="breakdown"></div>
    <div id="warnings"></div>

    <div class="block">
      <div class="block-h">
        <h3>Contribution room</h3>
        <span class="sub">Estimated from the income you entered</span>
      </div>
      <div class="dt-wrap" style="max-height:none">
        <table class="dt" style="min-width:460px"><thead><tr>
          <th>Account</th><th>Room</th><th>Used</th><th>Left</th>
        </tr></thead><tbody id="roomTable"></tbody></table>
      </div>
      <div class="assum">Room is estimated from the income you entered and ignores
      carry-forward and any pension adjustment. Your real figures are in CRA My Account.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="block">
      <div class="block-h">
        <h3>Why this order</h3>
        <span class="sub">What the solver is comparing</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ltext" style="max-width:none">
        <p>Each dollar is scored against what it earns you <em>this year</em>, then handed to
        whichever account scores highest, and the scoring is redone as your income falls:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Employer match</b> — the match rate itself, on top of the deduction. Nothing
          competes with an instant 50%.</li>
          <li><b>FHSA</b> — your full effective marginal rate, because it is deductible going in
          <em>and</em> tax-free coming out for a first home.</li>
          <li><b>RRSP</b> — your effective rate today minus the rate you expect to withdraw at.
          That difference is the whole bet, and it goes negative when you are contributing at a
          lower rate than you will withdraw at.</li>
          <li><b>TFSA</b> — no deduction, so it scores zero, but it is never negative. It is the
          baseline every other account has to beat.</li>
          <li><b>Regular account</b> — only once every registered dollar of room is used.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout">
          <span class="t">Why the effective rate, not your bracket</span>
          A deduction lowers your taxable income, which returns the tax <b>and</b> restores the
          income-tested benefits you were losing. For a family in a clawback band the benefit
          restored can exceed the refund. <a href="learn.html#marginal">How that works →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="callout warnbox">
          <span class="t">This assumes the groundwork is done</span>
          It cannot see your debts or your cash cushion. Clear high-interest debt and build an
          emergency fund first — both beat every allocation below.
          <a href="learn.html#order">The full order of operations →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

</div>
</div>

<footer>
  Federal brackets: CRA 2026. British Columbia brackets: Province of B.C. Canada Child Benefit,
  BC Family Benefit and Canada Groceries and Essentials Benefit: 2026–27 benefit year.
  Everything runs in your browser; nothing you type is sent anywhere or stored. The only thing kept on
  your device is whether you prefer the light or dark theme.
  <br><br>
  This is an educational model, not tax, financial, or investment advice. It does not account for
  every credit, deduction, or personal circumstance. Confirm your contribution room in CRA My Account,
  and consider speaking to a qualified professional before acting.
</footer>
